{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Enable a host firewall on node1 that permits inbound SSH and TCP port 8080 while rejecting unrelated inbound connections.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The active public zone is bound to enp1s0, allows only SSH and 8080/tcp, and has a REJECT target. Direct nftables inspection confirms accepts for TCP/22 and TCP/8080 followed by an administrative reject for unmatched input.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3cece5057c7c4fc7","cmd-784adfbf741d47b3","cmd-9bde5614ddef486a"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Make the host firewall configuration persistent.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before restart, firewalld was active and enabled and its runtime and permanent configurations matched. Acknowledged restart changed the boot identity; afterward the system recovered to running, firewalld and sshd were active, the SSH listener returned, and both runtime and permanent firewall rules retained SSH, 8080/tcp, and REJECT.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6bcc7098835b485c","cmd-869614374e604774","cmd-ed2ecd20ca704845","cmd-893052dc4ec64491","cmd-9bde5614ddef486a","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The sole configuration mutation added the required persistent 8080 allowance, retained SSH, removed unrelated ingress services, set REJECT, and reloaded firewalld; each change directly served the task (cmd-e0cfd1913ad34eb9). The reboot was required by the provider-wide restart protocol (cmd-869614374e604774). Failed polling commands were read-only observations during the restart. Final snapshots show no failed services, package damage, or abandoned temporary files attributable to the executor.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e0cfd1913ad34eb9","cmd-869614374e604774","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. node1 has an active, enabled, persistent firewalld policy allowing SSH and TCP/8080 and rejecting unmatched inbound traffic. The complete restart protocol was captured and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":["No external end-to-end packet probe was captured; permitted and rejected behavior is established through direct inspection of the active kernel nftables rules.","No application was listening on port 8080, so application reachability on that port was not tested; the firewall allowance itself was directly verified."]}
